{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376436-arcane-5-and-the-world-at-large","id":1376436,"title":"Arcane 5 and the world at large","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-24T14:46:09-07:00","id":1376436,"title":"Arcane 5 and the world at large","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> For M20, I have been told that maxing out Arcane it's counterproductive given that regular people would forget you too fast (emergency services forget you called, your landlord forgets that the place is already under your name, etc), so a lot of questions occur: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Does this anti-memetic effect extend to other supernaturals?</li> <li>How effective and fast is it on regular people? Could a Mage kidnap/maim/rape/steal from/shoot someone, leave the location and the victim would forget or invent a different memory of what happened?</li> <li>Will the Mind sphere protect people from the effect? If so, at what rating?</li> </ol><br /> Thanks for the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-24-2020, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T17:20:11-07:00","id":1376452,"title":"","content":"Arcane has limits regarding of the dot rating. The more memorable your actions, the more observers will remember; and the targets of your actions remember more details than onlookers. Arcane does not stop you from having friends and loved ones, it just takes more work to upkeep your relationships.<br /> <br /> Increased dots are not stated to act any faster, but memories are more confused by the effect. So the EMS issue doesn't really happen even if the EMTs will be confused about why they were called out and the dispatcher is going to lose the notes about what the emergency is, but high levels of Arcane do start causing problems for things like your landlord forgetting you exist and are living in your apartment. High Arcane works best with characters ready to live off the grid in a significant fashion.<br /> <br /> Arcane does work on supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Arcane will not cause the victim of a crime to forget what happened, or that you did it if they can still sense you. However when you're not around they'll get more and more fuzzy about the details that would identify you to others. They're not going to forget what happened even if they forget important details about you. If you have Arcane 5, and you shoot someone, they're not going to forget that someone just shot them. They might misremember the gun, what you were wearing, etc. though.<br /> <br /> I don't believe there's an official answer to this in M20, but there's no reason Mind can't be used to counter Arcane. Mind 1 has Mind Shields and Mental Empowerment that would both at least mitigate some of Arcane. That said, even mages that know about Arcane are stated to struggle to with any sort of permanent countermeasures. You might be able to protect your memories for the duration of a spell... but spells end, your attempts to record them get lost, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T18:35:37-07:00","id":1376459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376436-arcane-5-and-the-world-at-large?p=1376452#post1376452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;snip&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>^^All of this.<br /> <br /> I have also treated it as Obfuscate in a Vampire game. A character with a lower Auspex rating than the target's Arcane is affected, whereas one with equal or higher Auspex is unaffected. In Mage games, I have treated Arcane as passive countermagick to scrying spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Any technology distinguishable from magic is insufficiently advanced.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12101-nitromidas","name":"Nitromidas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T18:46:13-07:00","id":1376462,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376436-arcane-5-and-the-world-at-large?p=1376452#post1376452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcane has limits regarding of the dot rating. The more memorable your actions, the more observers will remember; and the targets of your actions remember more details than onlookers. Arcane does not stop you from having friends and loved ones, it just takes more work to upkeep your relationships.</div> </div> </div> </div>How can you have relationships if at Arcane 5 your significant other/partner starts forgetting your existence? Can you selectively choose people to be unaffected?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376436-arcane-5-and-the-world-at-large?p=1376452#post1376452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Increased dots are not stated to act any faster, but memories are more confused by the effect. So the EMS issue doesn't really happen even if the EMTs will be confused about why they were called out and the dispatcher is going to lose the notes about what the emergency is, but high levels of Arcane do start causing problems for things like your landlord forgetting you exist and are living in your apartment. High Arcane works best with characters ready to live off the grid in a significant fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376436-arcane-5-and-the-world-at-large?p=1376452#post1376452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcane does work on supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the effect also work on other Mages too?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376436-arcane-5-and-the-world-at-large?p=1376452#post1376452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcane will not cause the victim of a crime to forget what happened, or that you did it if they can still sense you. However when you're not around they'll get more and more fuzzy about the details that would identify you to others. They're not going to forget what happened even if they forget important details about you. If you have Arcane 5, and you shoot someone, they're not going to forget that someone just shot them. They might misremember the gun, what you were wearing, etc. though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would people also loose your fingerprints/shed skin/hair/semen/blood samples? Arcane + Spheres would make you a really hard to catch criminal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376436-arcane-5-and-the-world-at-large?p=1376452#post1376452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe there's an official answer to this in M20, but there's no reason Mind can't be used to counter Arcane. Mind 1 has Mind Shields and Mental Empowerment that would both at least mitigate some of Arcane. That said, even mages that know about Arcane are stated to struggle to with any sort of permanent countermeasures. You might be able to protect your memories for the duration of a spell... but spells end, your attempts to record them get lost, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems hard to counter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-24-2020, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T18:59:43-07:00","id":1376466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nitromidas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376436-arcane-5-and-the-world-at-large?p=1376459#post1376459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ^^All of this.<br /> <br /> I have also treated it as Obfuscate in a Vampire game. A character with a lower Auspex rating than the target's Arcane is affected, whereas one with equal or higher Auspex is unaffected. In Mage games, I have treated Arcane as passive countermagick to scrying spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it is countermagic in a way, but it wont stop a persistent Mage using a drawn out ritual to stack up enough success to surpass it.<br /> <br /> As far as to Ibeaumanior's question about relationships the answer is simple. You dont. A high Arcane is as much a curse as it is a benifit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 03-24-2020, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T20:27:58-07:00","id":1376475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376436-arcane-5-and-the-world-at-large?p=1376462#post1376462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the effect also work on other Mages too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. In fact, that's one of its bigger attractions for Tradition mages.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T23:01:21-07:00","id":1376485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376436-arcane-5-and-the-world-at-large?p=1376462#post1376462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can you have relationships if at Arcane 5 your significant other/partner starts forgetting your existence? Can you selectively choose people to be unaffected?</div> </div> </div> </div>Effectively. The more effort you put into being part of someone's life, the lower the impact of Arcane, and you can suppress it temporarily in general. It's basically a matter of repetition and reinforcement.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the effect also work on other Mages too? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would people also loose your fingerprints/shed skin/hair/semen/blood samples? </div> </div> </div>Probably. It does impact Investigation rolls and this would be a good explanation of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Arcane + Spheres would make you a really hard to catch criminal. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Though Spheres already make you really hard to catch. Time mages are a big counter to high Arcane mages trying to be bad. Arcane isn't perfect, and since the Traditions and Technocracy are aware of it, they do what they can to have countermeasures to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems hard to counter. </div> </div> </div>In a pure mechanical sense, Mental Empowerment can provide dice to the rolls Arcane penalizes as a direct counter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T05:46:51-07:00","id":1376528,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> thanks for your answers, the last one (I think), you mentioned: &quot;<i>Arcane will not cause the victim of a crime to forget what happened, or that you did it if they can still sense you.</i>&quot; What happens if you commit a crime, go and return later, do people memories about you get restored or are still fuzzy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T10:02:41-07:00","id":1376575,"title":"","content":"Fuzzy, but they'd probably still recognize you (even if they'd sound crazy, even to themselves, as you'd look nothing like they remembered). Remember that Arcane is supposed to be mediated by the impact you had. A high Arcane character that shoplifted can probably return to the scene of the crime relatively safely, because the security guard or shop owner are unlikely to be majorly shocked by this happening. Brutally torturing and maiming someone for the sadistic point of causing pain is likely to completely negate Arcane (at least for the victim's memory of what happened and you).<br /> <br /> There's no strict mechanical guide here, but the idea is that you can't just take Arcane for granted. To get the maximum effect you have to work with it,not against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T11:40:04-07:00","id":1486786,"title":"","content":"A bit of necromancy, but how will an Arcane 5 person deal with a day job?<br /> <br /> I am thinking of two scenarios:<br /> <br /> 1. The company forgets to pay you and to register you for all legal stuff (retirement plan, bonuses, etct)<br /> 2. The company forgets you exist and you keep being paid without really working there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T14:08:38-07:00","id":1486797,"title":"","content":"What's your job?<br /> <br /> Like, if your a cook at a small family restaurant where you're good buddies with the owner and manager? Arcane probably doesn't matter. You don't interact with people, you're not some celebrity chef people are coming just to try you latest masterpiece, you don't rely on tips, you just make the food and management is responsible for making sure it gets to tables and you get paid.<br /> <br /> If you're a cog in a giant corporate machine, the odds of you getting lost in the bureaucracy increase. When your shift supervisor is in charge of thirty people and barely knows any names as it is, you haven't seen anyone from HR in person since you were hired, and so on, keeping that job (and paycheck) requires the system to remember you because otherwise nobody else would, and Arcane makes the system forget about you.<br /> <br /> Then of course, there's just taking cash for illegal work where records are explicitly not part of the process. If your day job is being a faceless worker in an illegal drug lab where everyone gets handed a wad of cash at the end of the day, Arcane isn't going to matter.<br /> <br /> Or you could be Banksy where the mystery of your public persona generates Fame and Resources because nobody knows who you are except for a small group of closely trusted people that handle certain parts of the business of art for you. But you can walk down the street and nobody will know who you are, nobody will care, and so on.<br /> <br /> To repeat myself: you get the best results when you work with Arcane instead of fighting it. Day jobs can work with Arcane 5, or work against Arcane 5, and how well that plays out is going to follow the same line of thinking.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T16:28:50-07:00","id":1486806,"title":"","content":"I have a mage with Arcane 5 who works as a medical examiner. I paid 4 Background points for Certification so his MD doesn't just vanish from the system without a trace, but lots of his records do happen to get lost/corrupted. While his boss and some co-workers are among the &quot;few he can trust&quot; listed in the background who don't forget his existence, I figure he has to explain who he is and present ID even to police officers he's worked with on scene many times before. Generally it causes lots of inconvenience and irritation, as the trade-off for making it very difficult for his enemies to track him down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T16:43:35-07:00","id":1486810,"title":"","content":"This is how Tony Todd's character in the Final Destination movies can constantly talk to teenagers about Death trying to kill people that violated fate, sometimes in the middle of an active emergency scene, and nobody else seems to care that he does this on a regular basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T17:03:14-07:00","id":1486812,"title":"","content":"Arcane seems to be related to the Mists and the Fog. It erodes and twists memories. When we are shown incidents of levels of Arcane above Five these people often are no longer able to be in contact with the world around them. Arcane five doesn't just erode memory it's stated to cause accidents that cause records to be lost. Evidence degrades or transforms. Generally this isn't a high speed thing. <br /> <br /> A mage with Arcane 5 publicly committing murder in the street could and probably would be arrested. But their case might not get to trial. If they were sentenced to prison, they'd probably end up being able to simply leave after a time because no one would be able to prove why they're in prison in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T19:44:08-07:00","id":1486831,"title":"","content":"As most of editions have tried really hard to point out: being obvious removes the protection the Background offers. Killing someone on the street with lots of witnesses that you are the person that did it, means everyone that witnesses it (and all devices that recorded it) will identify you. The books note that overtime some blurring will occur, but the witnesses will still see you for who you are. Investigators might get different takes on the length of your hair, or the style of your shirt, but all of them will be able to pick you out of a lineup. Video recordings will be like the JFK assassination: capturing a lot, and all of them capturing things some do and others do, but because you're being obvious, not enough to cause doubt in a jury. You're also probably famous now, so your Fame rating is going to ensure that even if people don't remember jack shit about what you look like, guards are going to make sure the 4th Street Wacko is in their cell because nobody wants to deal with being the one that let a high profile prison get shanked in the bathroom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T06:31:32-07:00","id":1486875,"title":"","content":"Mind 1 can be used to counter Arcane, to counter the Fog caused by the Dream, Delirium and any other type of supernatural mental blurring","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T06:37:39-07:00","id":1486876,"title":"","content":"With Arcane 10 you would indeed be forgotten, even if you had murdered the president of the USA.<br /> <br /> In fact, JFK could perfectly had been assassinated by a Arcane 10 mage in perfect plain sight, and nobody would be any wiser about said person.<br /> <br /> Arcane 10 however is an insanely weird and extreme curse. You literally do not exist for the world, and you'll even &quot;fade away&quot; from existance entirely a few minutes each day; I would shitty my pants if I that happened constantly to me.<br /> <br /> And perhaps, some Arcane 10 guys simply disappear alltogheter, being completely erased from history - even from the past. Who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T13:37:38-07:00","id":1486906,"title":"","content":"I think that Arcane functions like a mid level conjuctive effect of Entropy and Mind. But it's not Vulgar. It's slow subtle and hard to spot even by those who know what to look for. So, for level 5 Arcane, if a Entropy 3/ Mind 3/ Prime 2 Coincidental rote could erase the evidence, then it will be erased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T19:25:36-07:00","id":1522984,"title":"","content":"Arcane of five makes me forget about this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T07:51:48-07:00","id":1523412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376436-arcane-5-and-the-world-at-large?p=1486812#post1486812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcane seems to be related to the Mists and the Fog. It erodes and twists memories. When we are shown incidents of levels of Arcane above Five these people often are no longer able to be in contact with the world around them. Arcane five doesn't just erode memory it's stated to cause accidents that cause records to be lost. Evidence degrades or transforms. Generally this isn't a high speed thing.<br /> <br /> A mage with Arcane 5 publicly committing murder in the street could and probably would be arrested. But their case might not get to trial. If they were sentenced to prison, they'd probably end up being able to simply leave after a time because no one would be able to prove why they're in prison in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Arcane 5 Mage sent to prison would probably get a &quot;life sentence&quot; since everybody would just keep forgetting why he was there, and every time anybody noticed his presence, they would start an investigation of who the hell that guy is, and then in the process of that they would forget him, only to accidentally notice his presence, restart the investigation that will lead nowhere from scratch, and the poor mage will forever be caught in that loop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T07:54:51-07:00","id":1523414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376436-arcane-5-and-the-world-at-large?p=1486906#post1486906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Arcane functions like a mid level conjuctive effect of Entropy and Mind. But it's not Vulgar. It's slow subtle and hard to spot even by those who know what to look for. So, for level 5 Arcane, if a Entropy 3/ Mind 3/ Prime 2 Coincidental rote could erase the evidence, then it will be erased.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why Prime 2?<br /> <br /> Arcane would be more like Entropy 5 than anything else. Lower levels don't really cut it.<br /> <br /> Entropy 5 could be used to lower or increase Arcanum, and with enough successes, make the change permanent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}